{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnJ53TSsYgxPGYAuJouF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All seven amended rows changed meaning, not just wording. I would bless six of them; I'm returning LLR-153 because it doesn't state a refusal its own test case checks. The verdict is committed as `1a00dcd6d` with the `WI: WI-993` and `Loop-Session` trailers. Only the verdict file is in the commit; the `.requested` file is still uncommitted.\n\n**Why each row is a meaning change:**\n- **LLR-118, LLR-299, TC-123, TC-314:** \"queued\" became \"queued or claimed.\" An open item cited only by a claimed work item used to be reported as an error; now it clears the error and shows as a card.\n- **LLR-153:** adds a fourth trigger. When an accepted verdict on a rung held for the owner rules a row MEANING, the mint now files an owner row and an open item, and that row leaves the amendment row.\n- **LLR-364:** what was \"the trunk mint\" is now \"the settled filter\", and it adds the sentence that an owner row carries such a record out of the amendment row.\n- **TC-147:** a full set of new checks for the new trigger.\n\n**Blessed (`[MEANING+BLESS]`):** LLR-118, LLR-299, LLR-364, TC-123, TC-147 and TC-314. Each new clause has a matching test, and the four test files they name passed: 91 passed in 72s.\n\n**Returned (`[MEANING]`): LLR-153.**\n- **Missing refusal:** when the open-items registry isn't in TOML format, the mint refuses by name and writes nothing, not even the amendment row, and the merge stands. TC-147 and `test_a_non_toml_registry_refuses_and_the_merge_stands` check this, but the row's text says \"every other state writes nothing\" and never says it refuses.\n- **Wording:** one sentence (\"…is named beside them\") doesn't say who does the naming. It should say the open item tells the owner to name any other unanchored rows.\n- **Fix drafted:** the `## Dispositions` section in the verdict file has a one-cell fix for LLR-153's `detail` with no code change, and it parses cleanly.\n\n**What this means for the follow-up act:**\n- **Test-case registry (TC-123, TC-147, TC-314):** can be re-attested now.\n- **Design registry (LLR-118, LLR-299, LLR-364):** has to wait until LLR-153 is judged again. Re-attesting them copies the whole design registry, which would include LLR-153's unblessed text.\n- **No owner sign-off needed:** none of these rows sits on a rung held for the owner.\n\nI also noted, without returning it, that the carry-out rule is now stated in both LLR-153 and LLR-364."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":553,"cache_read_input_tokens":94615,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":553},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5137c86e-cf2b-4214-969c-76a09f60f9fd","uuid":"70fdf194-eb05-4ffa-8178-2bd115069f43","timestamp":"2026-11-06T20:20:36.394Z","request_id":"req_011CgnJ53Jm2tKDLDec6yGpr"}
